<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>{{ t("add.page.add-targum", "Add — targum") }}</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('reader.css') }}{{ asset('chrome.css') }}{{ asset('add.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
<script>{{ asset('keep.js') }}</script>
{#- The key, before anything that reads it (targum-internal#343). `building.js`, and
    the conversation's pill, the followed series and the palette in the nav, each read `window.TARGUM_KEY`
    once as they load; it was set in a script at the foot of the body, so on a local serve
    they held an empty key for the life of the page and the bell, the followed series and
    the chat list were refused. The hosted box has no key and was never affected. -#}
<script>window.TARGUM_KEY = "{{ token }}";</script>
</head>
<body class="add">
{% set here = 'add' %}
{% include '_nav.html.j2' %}
<script>{{ asset('building.js') }}</script>
<main class="add-main">
  {#- This page used to be the front door and opened by saying what targum is. Reached
      from the nav by somebody who already has an account and a shelf, that reads as a
      stranger's greeting to a regular. It says what it is for instead. -#}
  <h1 class="lede">{{ t("add.page.add", "Add") }}</h1>
  {#- Worth a look before waiting for a build, and no more than that: the catalogue is a
      few hundred texts, not most of what anybody wants. -#}
  <p class="hint">{{ t("add.page.it-may-already-be-in-the", "It may already be in the") }}
    <a class="to-library" href="/library">{{ t("add.page.library", "Library") }}</a>.</p>

  {% if no_key %}
  <p class="notice" role="status">{{ no_key }}</p>
  {% endif %}

  {#- One box, for any medium (design.md §12, 2026-09-13, targum-internal#249). It was
      three boxes to choose between — a file, a link, the text — with a Translation and a
      Transcript toggle and two language pickers asked before anything had been read. The
      box takes whatever it is given and a line under it says what targum thinks that
      was; every choice the form had is behind Change. -#}
  {% include '_glyphs.html.j2' %}
  <section class="bring" aria-label="{{ t("add.page.what-to-add", "What to add") }}">
    <div class="drop" id="drop">
      <ul class="given-files" id="given-files" hidden></ul>
      <label class="given-label" for="given">{{ t("add.page.what-would-you-like-to-read", "What would you like to learn from?") }}</label>
      <textarea id="given" rows="2" dir="auto" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="understood"
                placeholder="{{ t("add.page.paste-a-link-or-some-hebrew-drop", "Paste a link or some Hebrew, drop a file, or say what you want") }}"></textarea>
      <p class="understood" id="understood" aria-live="polite">{{ t("add.page.we-can-read-books-articles-podcasts-videos", "We can read books, articles, podcasts, videos, voice notes, subtitles and photos of pages.") }}</p>
    </div>
    <input type="file" id="file" multiple
           accept=".txt,.md,.markdown,.epub,.pdf,.srt,.vtt,.png,.jpg,.jpeg,.webp,.heic,.heif,.mp3,.m4a,.m4b,.aac,.ogg,.opus,.flac,.wav,.mp4,.m4v,.mov,.webm,.mkv" hidden>
    <div class="bring-row">
      <button type="button" id="choose" class="bring-choose"><svg class="glyph" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#glyph-file"/></svg><span>{{ t("add.page.choose-files", "Choose files") }}</span></button>
      {#- Only for a description, and only where the talk drawer is there to say it in:
          looking for a text by describing it is a turn of conversation, metered like one,
          and the reader's own press sends it. -#}
      <button type="button" id="ask-targum" class="bring-ask" hidden>{{ t("add.page.ask-targum", "Ask targum") }}</button>
      {#- Paused where nothing new can be made (2026-09-14): the notice above said so and
          the button went on offering, and a press only repeated the notice. -#}
      <button type="button" id="go" class="go"{% if no_key %} disabled{% endif %}>{{ t("add.page.continue", "Continue") }}</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- What the box understood, and every choice on one line. -#}
  <div class="summary" id="summary" hidden>
    <p class="summary-line" id="summary-line"></p>
    <button type="button" id="change" class="change" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="options">{{ t("add.page.change", "Change") }}</button>
  </div>

  {#- The manual page: the controls the form had, with the ids they had, so a reader who
      knows exactly what they brought is never asked to trust a guess. Rows that do not
      apply to what is in the box are hidden. -#}
  <section class="options" id="options" aria-label="{{ t("add.page.choices", "Choices") }}" hidden>
    <div class="option-row">
      <h2>{{ t("add.page.languages", "Languages") }}</h2>
      <div class="option-body">
        <div class="pickers">
          {#- Three in and two out, each one saying how far along it is. Narrower than
              what the rest of the app can show: these are the pairs an upload has been
              taken end to end in. -#}
          <label class="field short">
            <span>{{ t("add.page.i-am-reading", "I'm learning") }}</span>
            <select id="from">
              {% for one in reading %}<option value="{{ one.code }}"{% if loop.first %} selected{% endif %}>{{ one.name }} ({{ one.label }})</option>{% endfor %}
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class="field short">
            <span>{{ t("add.page.translations-in", "Translations in") }}</span>
            {# No `selected` here: which language you read into is a choice you have
               already made, and `add.js` restores it. Marking the first one selected made
               the page forget it on every visit, which for anyone who reads into anything
               but English was a wrong answer waiting to be submitted. -#}
            <select id="to">
              {% for one in into %}<option value="{{ one.code }}">{{ one.name }} ({{ one.label }})</option>{% endfor %}
            </select>
          </label>
        </div>
        <p class="hint" id="from-beta" hidden></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {#- A translation the reader already has is a translation nobody has to make. The
        aligner lines it up sentence by sentence, the same way the catalogue's published
        translations are lined up. -#}
    <div class="option-row" id="translation-row">
      <h2>{{ t("add.page.translation", "Translation") }}</h2>
      <div class="option-body">
        <div class="segmented" id="how" role="group" aria-label="{{ t("add.page.where-the-translation-comes-from", "Where the translation comes from") }}">
          <button type="button" class="segment" data-how="make" aria-pressed="true">{{ t("add.page.we-ll-make-one", "We'll make one") }}</button>
          <button type="button" class="segment" data-how="mine" aria-pressed="false">{{ t("add.page.i-have-one", "I have one") }}</button>
        </div>
        <p class="hint" id="how-note">{{ t("add.page.we-ll-translate-it-sentence-by-sentence", "We'll translate it, sentence by sentence.") }}</p>
        <div id="have-translation" hidden>
          <div class="drop small" id="drop-translation" tabindex="0">
            <p class="drop-label">{{ t("add.page.drop-the-translation", "Drop the translation") }}</p>
            <p class="drop-note">{{ t("add.page.plain-text-or-markdown-in-reading-order", "Plain text or markdown, in reading order") }}</p>
            <input type="file" id="translation" accept=".txt,.md,.markdown,.epub" hidden>
            <button type="button" id="choose-translation">{{ t("add.page.choose-file", "Choose file") }}</button>
            <button type="button" id="unchoose-translation" class="unchoose" hidden>{{ t("add.page.something-else", "Something else") }}</button>
          </div>
          <label class="field">
            <textarea id="pasted-translation" rows="3" dir="auto" spellcheck="false"
                      placeholder="{{ t("add.page.or-paste-the-translation", "Or paste the translation") }}"></textarea>
          </label>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {#- Only when the box holds a recording. A transcript with its own timings makes the
        import free of transcription; without one, targum writes down what is said, part
        by part, as each part is asked for. -#}
    <div class="option-row" id="audio-extra" hidden>
      <h2>{{ t("add.page.transcript", "Transcript") }}</h2>
      <div class="option-body">
        <div class="segmented" id="spoken-how" role="group" aria-label="{{ t("add.page.where-the-transcript-comes-from", "Where the transcript comes from") }}">
          <button type="button" class="segment" data-spoken="make" aria-pressed="true">{{ t("add.page.we-ll-write-one", "We'll write one") }}</button>
          <button type="button" class="segment" data-spoken="mine" aria-pressed="false">{{ t("add.page.i-have-one", "I have one") }}</button>
        </div>
        <p class="hint" id="spoken-note">{{ t("add.page.we-ll-write-down-what-s-said", "We'll write down what's said, part by part.") }}</p>
        <div id="have-transcript" hidden>
          <div class="drop small" id="drop-transcript" tabindex="0">
            <p class="drop-label">{{ t("add.page.drop-the-transcript", "Drop the transcript") }}</p>
            <p class="drop-note">{{ t("add.page.srt-or-vtt-timings-kept", "SRT or VTT, timings kept") }}</p>
            <input type="file" id="transcript" accept=".srt,.vtt" hidden>
            <button type="button" id="choose-transcript">{{ t("add.page.choose-file", "Choose file") }}</button>
            <button type="button" id="unchoose-transcript" class="unchoose" hidden>{{ t("add.page.something-else", "Something else") }}</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- The library answering while the box is typed in (targum-internal#251): a text
      already here is said before Continue, not after a price for making a second copy
      of it. Drawn by `add.js`; empty and out of the way until it has something. -#}
  <div class="already" id="already" hidden></div>

  <div class="status" id="status" hidden></div>

  {#- What the hours are, before any of them are spent (targum-internal#299). The reader
      was told "a recording or a video uses some of your hours" and never what they had,
      so the first time anybody met the number was the month they ran out of it. Filled
      by `add.js` from `/account/me`, and absent where this install has no allowance to
      quote — an admin, or a machine somebody runs themselves. Time and not price, and
      the library named as costing none of it (§6, and the voice of 2026-09-13). -#}
  <p class="hint hours" id="hours" hidden></p>

  {#- The refusals, named before they are met, until each is said where it happens with
      the way on (targum-internal#252). -#}
  <p class="hint limits">{{ t("add.page.we-can-t-add-scanned-pdfs-protected", "We can't add scanned PDFs, protected audiobooks (.aax), Spotify or
    anything behind a login. A recording or a video uses some of your hours.") }}</p>

</main>
{% include '_foot.html.j2' %}
<script>
window.TARGUM_KEY = "{{ token }}";
window.TARGUM_LANGUAGES = { {% for code, name in languages %}"{{ code }}": "{{ name }}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} };
{#- `tojson` rather than quoting these by hand: an ampersand written into a script block
    comes out as `&amp;`, and "R&D" stopped matching itself. -#}
window.TARGUM_READING = {{ reading|tojson }};
window.TARGUM_INTO = {{ into|tojson }};
{% if strings %}window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};
{% endif %}</script>
<script>{{ asset('strings.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('lang.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('sync.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('account.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('bring.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('add.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
